    "narrative": "For the September 4th slate, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40), who projects as our premier start. Facing Ranger Suarez, **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits from a significant park factor boost and a favorable platoon dynamic, making him the highest-scoring asset in the lineup. **Kyle Tucker** (73.09) follows closely, buoyed by a soft matchup against Jackson Kent (5.48 xERA), providing the ideal profile of an elite hitter against a vulnerable arm. We are also expecting high-leverage production from **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.84) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.27), both of whom take advantage of favorable platoon splits to stabilize our baseline production across the 5x5 categories.\n\nThe optimization process yielded a difficult decision regarding our bench, with **Nasim Nunez** (41.04) narrowly missing the cut. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the elite sprint speed we covet for our stolen base deficit and benefits from a slow opposing pitcher delivery, his projected ninth-order position hampered his scoring floor. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher-order stability of **Wade Meckler**, despite his lower ceiling, to ensure more plate appearances against Jared Jones. We are monitoring **Drake Baldwin** closely today; while his score (48.99) is buoyed by leadoff assumptions, the 2.81 xERA of Cristopher S\u00e1nchez presents a genuine risk of a sub-optimal day if the lineup placement shifts downward. Owners should track official lineups to confirm that **Drake Baldwin**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and the rest of the core are cemented in their projected slots, as any demotion in the order for our middle-of-the-pack starters could trigger a re-evaluation of our efficiency targets.",
